## Distribution. Set NODE_COOKIE to a real secret before starting: the node
## refuses to boot with the placeholder cookie. Distribution is bound to the
## loopback interface; expose it only behind a firewall (or over TLS
## distribution) if you actually need remote nodes. If you do not need
## clustering or a remote console, comment out -name and -setcookie to run
## without distribution at all.
-name ${NODE_NAME:-chappe_sip@127.0.0.1}
-setcookie ${NODE_COOKIE:-CHANGE_ME_SET_NODE_COOKIE}
-kernel inet_dist_use_interface {127,0,0,1}
## epmd (the port mapper the node registers with) listens on loopback only.
## An epmd started before this file is read (by the release script's
## nodetool ping, or another node) takes ERL_EPMD_ADDRESS from the
## environment instead: deploy/chappe_sip.env.example sets it too.
-env ERL_EPMD_ADDRESS 127.0.0.1

+K true
+A 16
